x699 write x698 2
x700 text "A file starts with zero or more `use \"path.a0\"` lines, relative to the file. The linker loads every used file once, orders them by dependency, and validates the result as one program with one namespace. Cycles are rejected. A function name defined in two files is rejected with both locations. Diagnostics on a linked program name the file and line they belong to."
x701 puts x699 x700
x702 call close x701 
x703 call open x702 10
x704 write x703 4
x705 write x704 2
x706 text "code"
x707 puts x705 x706
x708 call open x707 4
x709 write x708 2
x710 text "use \"ui.a0\"\nuse \"../examples/life.a0\"\nfn page io -> io\na call open p0 5\nb call close a\nret b\nend"
x711 puts x709 x710
x712 call close x711 
x713 call close x712 
x714 call close x713 
x715 call open x714 13
x716 write x715 4
x717 write x716 1
x718 text "editing"
x719 puts x717 x718
x720 call open x719 11
x721 write x720 2
x722 text "Views and edits"
x723 puts x721 x722
x724 call close x723 
x725 call open x724 2
x726 write x725 2
x727 text "A model never sees a whole file. It asks for a view of one function: the function with a handle line on top (e0) and, when the whole program matters, a program handle (g0) with one signature line per function. A reply is the handle line followed by edits, one per line: `id op ...` replaces the instruction id or inserts it before ret; `id op ... @ other` inserts after other; `-id` deletes; `ret x` changes the result. Under g0, a whole `fn ... end` block adds or replaces a function and `-fn name` removes one. The edit is applied only if it parses, type-checks, validates, and was written against the current revision; otherwise it is rejected and the handle stays valid."
x728 puts x726 x727
x729 call close x728 
x730 call open x729 10
x731 write x730 4
x732 write x731 2
